former so the preprocessing flow is identical across candidates.</idea>\n<idea>Evaluate candidates with 5-fold StratifiedKFold inside the 712 training rows for stability plus the fixed 179-row validation as the decisive metric.</idea>\n<idea>Persist a comparison table (model, features, val acc) as an artifact; only the best model is finally serialized.</idea>\n</solution>\n\n<solution>\n<description>ROUND 4 — Error analysis, calibration and interpretability. Hypothesis: remaining errors concentrate in ambiguous cases — males in 1st/2nd class, boys in 3rd class, missing-Age adults, and rare titles. Plan: inspect misclassified validation rows (never their labels beyond the evaluator-exposed validation predictions we generate), bucket errors by Sex/Pclass/Age-missing, and test targeted fixes: (a) calibration check — sweep decision threshold only to diagnose, but keep the required 0.5 threshold for the reported metric; (b) if errors concentrate in a specific subgroup, try a targeted interaction feature (Sex×Pclass, Title×Pclass) or add Age bins; (c) report permutation importance / coefficients to confirm the model uses sensible signals. Only promote a change if it improves the fixed validation accuracy by >0.5 pp, i.e., not noise. Keep the best artifacts and the final predictions.csv produced by the same winning model.</description>\n<idea>Bucket validation errors by (Sex, Pclass, Age-isna) and print counts; flag any bucket where the model is systematically wrong.</idea>\n<idea>Add Sex×Pclass and Title×Pclass one-hot interactions and re-evaluate the winning model family; accept only if validation accuracy improves.</idea>\n<idea>Serialize the final Pipeline (preprocess+model) with joblib, save val_predictions.csv (PassengerId, Survived) and predictions.csv (418 rows, header, int 0/1, test order preserved), plus a metrics.json and README inference note.</idea>\n</solution>", role='assistant', tool_calls=None, function_call=None, provider_specific_fields=None), provider_s