Parch numeric + Age/Fare median impute (add missingness indicators) → LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, random_state=42); report val accuracy vs floors and log runtime.\n- ROUND 2 — Name/Ticket/Cabin/Family feature engineering on the same fixed split. Hypothesis: Title (Mr/Mrs/Miss/Master/Rare via regex r\',\\s*([A-Za-z]+)\\.\'), FamilySize=SibSp+Parch+1, IsAlone, Cabin deck letter, Ticket prefix and Fare-per-person add signal (women/children in higher classes survive more; large families less; Title proxies missing Age), lifting fixed validation accuracy by +1 to +3 pp over Round 1. Validation plan: identical 712/179 split, same LogisticRegression family, then a shallow DecisionTree (depth≤4) to probe non-linearity; accept only if fixed validation accuracy improves. Impute missing Age using per-Title median computed on the 712 training rows only. All imputers/encoders fit on training rows only; transform validation/test. Runtime a few seconds, CPU.\n- Build a featurize(df) function adding FamilySize, IsAlone, Title (normalize Mlle/Ms→Miss, Mme→Mrs, rare→Rare) and a Cabin deck letter; apply identically to train/val/test.\n- Add per-Title median Age imputation + Age-missing indicator fit on training rows only; compare LR val accuracy vs Round 1 baseline.\n- Fit a shallow DecisionTreeClassifier(max_depth=4, random_state=42) on the engineered set as a non-linearity probe; record val accuracy in a comparison table.\n- ROUND 3 — Model comparison under the fixed split, sharing one ColumnTransformer. Hypothesis: tree ensembles (HistGradientBoostingClassifier(max_iter=300), RandomForest n_estimators=400 with max_depth∈{4,6,8}, min_samples_leaf∈{1,3,5}, ≤12 combos per family) outperform the linear model on the engineered features, and a soft-vote of the best two is best. Validation plan: same fixed 179-row validation is decisive; run 5-fold StratifiedKFold inside the 712 training rows only for stability diagnostics; persist a comparison table (model, features, val acc) as an