training rows only): ColumnTransformer = Sex one-hot + Pclass/SibSp/Parch numeric + Age/Fare median impute with missingness indicators → LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000, random_state=42). Report validation accuracy vs majority floor (~0.615) and Sex-only rule (~0.776). Hypothesis: baseline lands ~0.81–0.82. This is the reference all later rounds compare to.\n- ROUND 2 — Confirmed feature set as the working baseline (already measured, keep as the standard). Evidence from round-001: raw LR ~0.816 → +Title/FamilySize/IsAlone ~0.8436 (best single model, L1-tuned LR). Feature engineering to keep identical across all rounds: FamilySize=SibSp+Parch+1, IsAlone=(FamilySize==1), Title from Name regex ", ([^.]+)." with Mlle/Ms→Miss, Mme→Mrs, rare→"Rare". Preprocessing in one shared ColumnTransformer fit on training rows only: StandardScaler on [Pclass,SibSp,Parch,FamilySize,IsAlone]; SimpleImputer(median, add_indicator=True)+StandardScaler on [Age,Fare]; SimpleImputer(constant \'M\')+OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\'ignore\') on [Sex,Embarked,Title]. Do not re-test variants already shown to regress (Deck, LogFare, AgeBin, class_weight, RF standalone) unless part of a new hypothesis; they added no gain in round-001.\n- ROUND 3 — Confirmed best: LR+ExtraTrees soft-vote (keep as incumbent, guard against noise). Evidence: 0.5*LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, random_state=42) + 0.5*ExtraTreesClassifier(n_estimators=400, max_depth=6, min_samples_leaf=4, random_state=42, n_jobs=4), proba≥0.5→1, scored 0.8492 vs 0.8436 single LR. Caveat from round-001: +0.56 pp on 179 rows is within noise (±1–2 pts). Treat 0.8492 as incumbent but do not treat it as decisively better than 0.8436. Any new candidate must beat 0.8492 on the fixed 179-row validation to replace the incumbent; also report an internal 5-fold StratifiedKFold accuracy on the 712 train rows as a stability diagnostic (do not tune on the fixed validation).\n- ROUND 4 — Re-tune blend weight and ExtraTrees leaf/depth via internal CV