fficients to confirm sensible signal use. Only if a bucket is systematically wrong, test one targeted interaction (Sex×Pclass or Title×Pclass) and accept only if fixed validation improves >0.5 pp beyond the CV-selected incumbent. Final deliverable: serialize the single winning Pipeline/blend (preprocess+model) via joblib; write work/val_predictions.csv (179 rows, PassengerId+Survived, aligned to validation.csv order), predictions.csv (418 rows, header, exactly PassengerId,Survived, int 0/1, test order preserved, no index), work/metrics.json (fixed-validation accuracy + CV diagnostics), and work/README.txt inference note stating proba≥0.5→1 and that validation and test predictions come from the same winning model.</ideas>\n<local_experiments>\n<experiment>\n<id>round-001-experiment-01</id>\n<title>Titanic Logistic Baseline</title>\n<description>Hypothesis: Titanic survival is largely driven by sex, class, age and family structure; a regularized linear model on well-engineered features (title extracted from Name, family size, alone flag) with median-imputed Age/Fare plus missing indicators would outperform a raw-feature baseline. A later soft-voting ensemble with ExtraTrees was tested and scored the highest.\n\nData processing:\n- Read local train_data/train.csv (712 labeled rows), validation_data/validation.csv (179 feature-only rows), predict_data/test.csv (418 rows). No external data, no gender_submission.csv.\n- Note: the fixed 179-row validation set is supplied pre-split (validation.csv); the earlier re-split of the 712-row train set produced 143 rows and failed evaluation. Corrected to train on all 712 rows and predict the supplied 179-row validation.csv by PassengerId.\n- Feature engineering (deterministic, fit-safe): FamilySize=SibSp+Parch+1, IsAlone=(FamilySize==1), Title from Name regex ", ([^.]+)." with Mlle/Ms→Miss, Mme→Mrs, rare→"Rare".\n- Preprocessing in a ColumnTransformer fit on training rows only: StandardScaler on numeric (Pclass,SibSp,Parch,FamilySize,IsAlone); Age/Fare median imputation with missing indicator then scaling; Sex/Embarked (missing→\'M\')/Title one-hot with handle_unknown=\'ignore\'.\n\nBest measured model:\n- 0.5 * LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, random_state=42) + 0.5 * ExtraTreesClassifier(n_estimators=400, max_depth=6, min_samples_leaf=4, random_state=42, n_jobs=4). Soft-vote of predict_proba, threshold ≥0.5 → 1. Seed 42, CPU.\n- This ensemble scored the engine-recorded best validation metric 0.8492, exceeding the single L1-regularized LR (C tuned, 0.8436) and the earlier RF (0.83), LogFare/wt/Deck/AgeBin variants (≤0.8436).\n\nValidation evidence (executed): The evaluator measured the fixed-split accuracy; the best reported is 0.8492 for the LR+ExtraTrees soft-vote. Single-factor results measured along the way: majority floor ~0.615, sex-only ~0.776, baseline LR ~0.816, +Title/FamilySize/IsAlone ~0.8436, RF ~0.832, LogFare ~0.832, class_weight ~0.827.\n\nChanges from parent: started from an LR baseline using raw Pclass/SibSp/Parch/Sex/Embarked with Age/Fare imputation. Added Name-derived Title, FamilySize, IsAlone, standardized numerics, and finally a soft-voting ExtraTrees ensemble.\n\nArtifacts: predictions.csv (418 rows, PassengerId+Survived, test order), work/val_predictions.csv (179 rows aligned to validation.csv), work/model_blend_et.joblib (dict {"lr","et"}), work/metrics.json, work/README.txt. Earlier single-model artifacts retained: work/model_final.joblib.\n\nLoad: joblib.load("work/model_blend_et.joblib"); prob = 0.5*lr.predict_proba(X)[:,1] + 0.5*et.predict_proba(X)[:,1]; Survived = (prob>=0.5).astype(int). Apply the same featurize() to raw rows before predict.</description>\n<code># featurize(df): add FamilySize, IsAlone, Title (Name regex; Mlle/Ms->Miss, Mme->Mrs, rare->Rare)\n# ColumnTransformer:\n#   num = SimpleImputer(median)+StandardScaler on [Pclass,SibSp,Parch,FamilySize,IsAlone]\n#   af  = SimpleImputer(median, add_indicator=True)+StandardScaler on [Age,Fare]\n#   cat = SimpleImputer(constant \'M\')+OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\'ignore\') on [Sex,Embarked,Title]\n# lr = Pipeline(pre, LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, random_state=42)).fit(X_tr,y_tr)\n# et = Pipeline(pre, ExtraTreesClassifier(n_estimators=400, max_depth=6, min_samples_leaf=4,\n#                                         random_state=42, n_jobs=4)).fit(X_tr,y_tr)\n# prob = 0.5*lr.predict_proba(X)[:,1] + 0.5*et.predict_proba(X)[:,1]\n# Survived = (prob>=0.5).astype(int)\n# val -> work/val_predictions.csv (aligned to validation.csv PassengerId order)\n# test -> predictions.csv (418 rows, header PassengerId,Survived, no index)\n# joblib.dump({"lr":lr,"et":et}, "work/model_blend_et.joblib")</code>\n<validation_metric>Metric↑(0.8492)</validation_metric>\n<suggestions>Observed weaknesses (evidence): The validation set is only 179 rows, so single-trial accuracy swings by ~1–2 points are within noise; the 0.8436→0.8492 gain from the ensemble is plausible but small and could partly be noise. RF, LogFare, class_weight, C-tuning, Deck and AgeBin added no gain; LR on the chosen features is a strong, stable baseline.\n\nLessons (evidence): (1) The validation set is supplied pre-split; do not re-split the 712-row train file (caused the 143-vs-179 failure). (2) Scaling numerics removed lbfgs convergence warnings without changing accuracy. (3) Tree ensembles only helped as a soft complement to LR (LR+ExtraTrees), not standalone (RF/GB regressed).\n\nPrioritized next experiments (hypotheses, not yet run): (1) Re-tune ExtraTrees depth/leaf and the LR/ET blend weight (0.5 fixed here) via internal 5-fold CV on the 712 train rows — test whether the blend weight and leaf size matter beyond noise. (2) Add a small calibrated HistGradientBoosting as a third voter with weight chosen by CV; verify it beats the two-model blend on the fixed 179-row validation. (3) Calibrate probabilities (Platt/isotonic on internal CV) to check if threshold 0.5 remains optimal for accuracy. (4) Confirm run-to-run stability by varying the ET n_jobs/seed-free components; keep seed 42 and report variance across internal CV folds rather than trusting a single fixed-split number.</suggestions>\n</experiment>\n\n\n<experiment>\n<id>round-002-experiment-01</id>\n<title>CV-tuned blend weights & ET leaves</title>\n<description>**Task & metric.** Binary classification of Titanic `Survived` (0/1). Primary metric is accuracy on the fixed 179-row validation holdout; training uses the evaluator-supplied 712 rows of `train_data/train.csv` only, validation/test are transform-only, and predictions must be 0/1 (prob >= 0.5 -> 1).\n\n**Best measured version (canonical incumbent, fixed-validation accuracy 0.8492 — the best score observed across all executed rounds).** A 50/50 soft-vote blend of two CPU models fit on all 712 training rows:\n- LogisticRegression (sklearn default C=1.0, max_iter=2000, random_state=42).\n- ExtraTreesClassifier(n_estimators=400, max_depth=6, min_samples_leaf=4, criterion=\'gini\', random_state=42, n_jobs=4).\n- Blended probability = 0.5*p_LR + 0.5*p_ET; Survived = 1 if prob >= 0.5 else 0.\n\n**Feature processing (shared ColumnTransformer fit on training rows only, embedded in each pipeline):**\n- `FamilySize = SibSp + Parch + 1`, `IsAlone = (FamilySize == 1)`.\n- `Title` extracted from `Name` via regex `,\\s*([^.]+)\\.`; Mlle/Ms -> Miss, Mme -> Mrs; titles with training count < 10 mapped to `Rare`.\n- `Embarked` missing -> \'M\'.\n- Numeric `[Pclass, SibSp, Parch, FamilySize, IsAlone]`: median impute + StandardScaler.\n- `[Age, Fare]`: median impute with add_indicator + StandardScaler.\n- Categorical `[Sex, Embarked, Title]`: constant \'M\' impute + OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown=\'ignore\').\n\n**Validation evidence (executed, evaluator-scored):**\n- Incumbent achieved 0.8492 on the fixed 179-row holdout (best so far; reproduced byte-identically, val md5 `cceba64816`, test md5 `42c718fef6`).\n- Seven controlled perturbations were each executed and all failed to beat 0.8492: round-4 CV-tuned blend (w=0.4, ET d=6/leaf=3) = 0.8436; interaction features (Sex_Pclass, FamilySize_bin) = 0.8212; LR+ET+GB 3-way vote = 0.8436; ET n_estimators 400->800 = 0.8436; decision threshold 0.45 = 0.8380; 5-seed bagging = 0.8436; CV-selected LR C=0.3 = 0.8380. ET criterion=\'entropy\' produced byte-identical predictions to gini (no change in metric). Each was reverted to the incumbent.\n\n**Changes from the parent.** The parent is the same LR+ExtraTrees soft-vote incumbent at w=0.5 with depth=6, leaf=4 (scored 0.8492). The best version is identical to the parent; all substantive changes attempted this round regressed, so the parent recipe was retained and re-verified.\n\n**Artifacts & loading (in `work/`):**\n- `work/model_blend_best.joblib`: dict with keys `lr`, `et` (full sklearn Pipelines including preprocessing), `w` (0.5), `n_estimators`, `threshold` (0.5), `lr_C` (1.0), `et_criterion` (\'gini\'). Load with `joblib.load("work/model_blend_best.joblib")`; predict via `w*lr.predict_proba(X)[:,1] + (1-w)*et.predict_proba(X)[:,1] >= threshold`, where `X` is the featurized DataFrame (FamilySize/IsAlone/Title/Embarked derived, raw columns selected).\n- `predictions.csv`: 418-row test predictions (PassengerId, Survived), original test order.\n- `work/val_predictions.csv`: 179-row validation predictions aligned to validation order.\n- `work/metrics.json`: config, metric 0.8492, full perturbation ledger, pinned md5s.\n- `work/README.txt`: inference instructions.\n\n**Reproducibility.** Seed 42, CPU, n_jobs=4, no downloads; val/test predictions come from the same single model and were asserted byte-identical to the pinned md5s on reload.</description>\n<code># --- Best measured pipeline (canonical incumbent) ---\nimport joblib, numpy as np, pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\nfrom sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler, OneHotEncoder\nfrom sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\nfrom sklearn.ensemble import ExtraTreesClassifier\n\nSEED = 42\n# 1) load train/val/test (relative to ../input/data/)\n# 2) featurize: FamilySize, IsAlone, Title(rare<10->Rare via training counts), Embarked missing->\'M\'\n#    (same featurize applied to train/val/test; rare mapping computed from training Title counts only)\n# 3) shared ColumnTransformer:\n#      num[Pclass,SibSp,Parch,FamilySize,IsAlone] -> median impute + StandardScaler\n#      af [Age,Fare]                              -> median impute(add_indicator) + StandardScaler\n#      cat[Sex,Embarked,Title]                    -> constant \'M\' impute + OneHotEncoder(ignore)\n#    embedded in each Pipeline so preprocessing is fit inside the model pipeline on training rows only.\nlr = Pipeline([("pre", make_pre()), ("lr", LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, random_state=SEED))]).fit(X, y)\net = Pipeline([("pre", make_pre()), ("et", ExtraTreesClassifier(\n        n_estimators=400, max_depth=6, min_samples_leaf=4,\n        criterion="gini", random_state=SEED, n_jobs=4))]).fit(X, y)\n# 4) blend: prob = 0.5*lr.proba + 0.5*et.proba ; Survived = (prob >= 0.5)\n# 5) write predictions.csv (418) and work/val_predictions.csv (179) from this single model;\n#    persist joblib.dump({"lr","et","w":0.5,"threshold":0.5,...}, "work/model_blend_best.joblib")\n# 6) assert val/test PassengerId alignment, 0/1 domain, and reload-reproducibility.\n\n# Failed approach summary: 7 perturbations (CV blend tuning, interaction features, 3-way GB vote,\n# more trees, threshold 0.45, seed-bagging, LR C=0.3) each executed and regressed below 0.8492;\n# entropy criterion gave identical predictions. All were reverted to the incumbent.</code>\n<validation_metric>Metric↑(0.8492)</validation_metric>\n<suggestions>**Observed weaknesses (evidence):**\n- The 179-row holdout is tiny; a single row is worth ~0.0056 accuracy, so perturbations move the score by only 1-4 rows and are dominated by noise. Round-4 and round-18 CV gains on 712 rows (+0.003 to +0.007 in 5-fold) failed to transfer to the holdout (both scored ~0.838-0.844) — CV-based selection is not a reliable proxy here.\n- Every added feature/model complexity (interactions, GradientBoosting, seed bagging, stronger ET) regressed; the incumbent is a stable optimum on this specific holdout.\n- Threshold and criterion changes either regressed (0.45) or were prediction-identical (entropy), implying the model\'s decision boundary is already saturated for these features.\n\n**Prioritized next experiments (hypotheses, not yet demonstrated):**\n1. Genuine new signal, not model tuning: the strongest untested Titanic predictor is likely `Cabin` deck (first letter), currently dropped. A fit-safe deck feature (missing -> \'U\') could add real information the current feature set lacks — test as a single controlled addition over the incumbent.\n2. Family/ticket-group survival features: shared `Ticket` prefix and group-size interactions sometimes carry signal; test one at a time and only keep if it beats 0.8492 on the fixed holdout (guard against the observed overfitting-on-179 pattern).\n3. If further tuning is pursued, consider that the evaluator\'s 712/179 split is the only reliable measuring stick — do not trust internal CV for final selection, since two CV-selected configs both regressed.\n4. Do NOT re-run already-rejected perturbations (interactions, GB, more trees, threshold shift, seed-bag, LR C, criterion) — they have executed negative evidence.\n\n**Lesson:** On this holdout the incumbent LR+ET (w=0.5, d=6, leaf=4) is the reproducible best; future rounds should either accept it as final or justify a *new-information* feature (e.g., Cabin deck) with a single controlled test rather than more hyperparameter search.</suggestions>\n</experiment>\n\n<failed_attempts></failed_attempts></local_experiments>\nThe business requirements define the target, primary metric, validation rules,\npermitted inputs and output schema. Use only supplied local data and completed\nlocal experiments. Do not download datasets, pretrained models or predictions.\nStart with a simple reproducible baseline. Keep the evaluator\'s split fixed,\nfit preprocessing on training rows only, and never read hidden validation labels.\nEvery improvement needs a testable hypothesis and comparable validation evidence.\nTreat failed and unscored attempts as lessons, not successful results.\nUse CPU when a library lacks support for the selected accelerator.\n\nPropose at least four feasible solution paths. On the first round prioritize a\ncheap baseline and data-quality checks. On later rounds identify weaknesses in\nmeasured local results, avoid repeating failed attempts, and propose controlled\nchanges with a hypothesis, expected evidence, runtime and memory cost.\nInclude error analysis, calibration or interpretability when business goals need them.\nRespond using repeated tags:\n<solution><description>Approach, hypothesis and validation plan</description>\n<idea>One concrete implementation step</idea><idea>Another step</idea></solution>\n'}]
